;;; A probe, not a corpus program: an obligation with no `absent`. The corpus
;;; writes one, `o` of examples/ein-bugs/wrong-answers/macro-eq-obligation.ein,
;;; in a file that is refused for another reason.
;;; It loads. Every state that holds (a K) owes, and nothing can pay: there is
;;; no witness to find. A requirement that asks no question.

(relation a T :why "{?3} is an a")
(a K)
(rule o ()
  :match  (a ?x)
  :assert (open)
  :why    "{?x} is an a, so the state owes")
